## The double-ended queue

capability deque/make  an empty double-ended queue, or one over a list held
  heroes  containers.new_deque, containers.deque_over
  go      ring.New
  rust    VecDeque::new, VecDeque::default, VecDeque::from, VecDeque::from_iter, VecDeque::try_with_capacity
  python  collections.deque, deque.copy, deque.__copy__
  note    a ring over the program's item list that doubles when full and is cut back when three quarters stand empty; Go's `ring.New(n)` makes n links holding nothing, which with no `nil` here is `new_bounded_deque(n)`, the use it is put to. A copy is `=` of the shape and the list

capability deque/bounded  a deque that holds at most a number of items, the oldest dropped
  heroes  containers.new_bounded_deque, containers.deque_limit
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  deque.maxlen
  note    Python's: a push at one end of a full deque drops the item at the other, observed (`maxlen=3` after a to e gives c d e, then `appendleft("z")` gives z c d); an insert into a full one is refused `invalid`, as Python raises

