## The cache that forgets the least recently used

capability cache/make  a cache of a capacity, with a time to live or none
  heroes  containers.new_cache, containers.new_cache_with_ttl, containers.cache_capacity
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  functools.lru_cache, functools.cache
  note    time is the program's: every call that can expire takes `now` in the program's own unit and no clock is read, so a test needs none, and the package needs no `time`, whose use adds 2,098,016 bytes to a program (309,368 against 2,407,384, measured 2026-11-17). Python's `lru_cache` wraps a function; the function here is the program's, which asks `cache_get` and on `not_found` computes and calls `cache_put`. Java's LinkedHashMap in access order with `removeEldestEntry` is this

capability cache/put  a value put, the least recently used forgotten where the cache is full
